Package: cpgdirection
Type: Package
Title: Predict the Direction of CpG-Gene Expression Associations
Version: 2.6.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tsachi", "Ein-Dor", email = "teindor@runi.ac.il",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "fnd"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3078-7591")))
Description: Assigns a direction to the association between DNA methylation at a
    CpG site and the expression of a nearby gene, for CpGs that have no measured
    expression quantitative trait methylation (eQTM) record. Predictions come
    from a precomputed table of 3,105,697 CpG-gene pairs covering 761,445 CpGs,
    assembled from four sources of evidence: directly measured eQTMs, summary-data
    Mendelian randomisation using genetic instruments, gradient-boosted models of
    genomic context and local catalogue structure fitted separately in blood,
    nasal epithelium and solid tissue, and a distance prior. Each call returns a
    direction, a calibrated probability, an evidence tier and an expected
    accuracy, and abstains where the evidence is insufficient. Predictions
    estimate direction conditional on the CpG being an eQTM; they do not
    establish that an effect exists.
